<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Hulao</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">621</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transition-from-sui-to-tang">Transition from Sui to Tang</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Hulao was fought in 621 at the Hulao Pass, a fortified gap west of modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zhengzhou">Zhengzhou</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henan">Henan</a>, during the wars that followed the fall of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a>. The Tang prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-taizong-of-tang">Li Shimin</a>, besieging <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-shichong">Wang Shichong</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luoyang">Luoyang</a>, held the pass against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dou-jiande">Dou Jiande</a>'s relieving army, routed it and captured Dou. Wang Shichong surrendered soon after, and the victory gave the Tang control of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-china-plain">North China Plain</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-hulao.jpg" alt="Battle of Hulao" width="320" height="218" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SS · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Luoyang_Hulao.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
